Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||06-14-2000||06:18 AM||||I've just installed the Pioneer DEH-P77DH CD Receiver and I must say I like it <B>a lot</B>! The only problem is (as I mentioned in another topic) that the frequency spacing for the radio is different here in Europe than in the US. I gave Pioneer Electronics a call and they said there was no way to change this - but I wonder. My old radio supposedly couldn't be changed either and it turned out to be something simple: removing a diode inside.<P>Does anybody know if I could get the service manual from Pioneer? Will they give/sell it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||06-14-2000||09:03 AM||||Cliff, Have you tried  <A HREF="http://www.pioneerelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.pioneerelectronics.com</A> ?  There may be a customer service number to order the serice manual.  Also, you might try calling Crutchfields Tech support and telling them you are thinking of buying that model, but you wander what the options are because you live overseas.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||06-14-2000||09:09 AM||||Cliff, <P>Its a slow morning so I just called 1-800-PIONEER for you.  <P>The part number for the repair manual you want is CRT2455 and the cost is US$25.72.<P>Hope this helps!||||reg||1
